  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "timer-steer-telemetry-export",
    "parent": "timer-effect-steer",
    "kind": "enabling",
    "title": "Export timer_effects and timer_steer counters into the evaluation record",
    "description": "In spur-core/src/simulator/util_stats.rs and the explorer/campaign serialization path (simulator/explorer.rs, simulator/campaign.rs), add the timer_effect aggregate (fired/acted split by in-flight-delivery, keyed by resume vertex, plus inert-streak histogram) and the timer_steer.{evaluated, lowered, raised} counters to the same serialized utilStats object that already carries termination, deliveryEffects and steerAuthority, so any run of a timer-admission hypothesis reports whether the multiplier fired and whether idle acted_fraction moved. No scheduler behavior change; counters are always emitted (zero-cost when the gating config field is false). Also investigate why steerAuthority is all-zero in this record — if that block is stale/unwired, the same fix applies.",
    "category": "tooling",
    "buildsOn": [
      "util_stats",
      "timer_effect",
      "explorer serialization"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 4,
    "expectedCost": 1,
    "rationale": "The timer-effect-steer run could not be falsified on its own stated criterion because the counters it added never reached the evaluation record; every future timer-admission or steer-authority hypothesis has the same blind spot, and each blind re-run costs a full 300s sequential chunk.",
    "generalityArgument": "Pure telemetry plumbing over existing protocol-agnostic counters keyed by CFG vertex and delivery state; names no handler, message or spec.",
    "status": "proposed",
    "branch": null,
    "prUrls": [],
    "createdAtIso": "2026-08-29T15:40:00Z",
    "firingCounter": null,
    "notes": "Prerequisite for re-running timer-effect-steer or any variant; without it the falsifier is unevaluable. [rejudged iteration 5327: timer-effect-steer's declared falsifier was unobservable; timer_effects now shows up in utilization but timer_steer.{evaluated,lowered,raised} exists nowhere, so this is the cheap prerequisite that makes the late-budget variant falsifiable; counters only, no tunable, no"
  },
